	 ('Daratumumab (Dara) promotes monocyte activation, inducing an increase in T cell costimulatory molecules (CD86/80).',NULL,NULL,'2025-07-31 00:27:08.845306','https://clinical-lymphoma-myeloma-leukemia.com/retrieve/pii/S2152265019316313',NULL,NULL,'cd86_c57503ae45c976d6',NULL,'not_reviewed'::public.review_status_enum,NULL,NULL),
	 ('The study investigated the effect of methotrexate (MTX) on drug resistance-related cancer stem cell (CSC) markers in non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) cell lines. The results showed that MTX treatment significantly increased the expression of ABCG2, IL-6R, and CD133, indicating that MTX enhances the expression of drug-resistance related CSC markers in NSCLC cell lines.',NULL,NULL,'2025-07-31 16:20:31.210602','https://europepmc.org/articles/pmc3298820?pdf=render',NULL,NULL,'ccs_df50f3e85183b241',NULL,'not_reviewed'::public.review_status_enum,NULL,NULL),
	 ('The study investigated the effects of imatinib therapy on Gastrointestinal stromal tumors (GISTs). The research found that CD68-positivity in areas negative for KIT (CD117) suggested previous infiltration of monocytes/macrophages into these regions. The study indicates that chronic inflammation subsequent to imatinib treatment may determine monocyte/macrophage recruitment in imatinib-damaged areas.',NULL,NULL,'2025-08-02 03:26:45.361036','https://translational-medicine.biomedcentral.com/track/pdf/10.1186/1479-5876-9-158',NULL,NULL,'cd68_abfbb126b6ec196d',NULL,'not_reviewed'::public.review_status_enum,NULL,NULL),
	 ('The article discusses the effect of idelalisib on T-cell function in chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL). It mentions that idelalisib reduces the expression of receptors commonly induced during activation of T cells, including CD69 and CD25. The study used gene expression profile (GEP) analysis and found that idelalisib down-regulated several genes, including CD69. The role of CD68 is not mentioned in the context of Idelalisib treatment.',NULL,NULL,'2025-08-02 03:27:33.602539','https://haematologica.org/article/view/8718',NULL,NULL,'cd68_0353fa84dc7acd5a',NULL,'not_reviewed'::public.review_status_enum,NULL,NULL),
	 ('The study investigated the effect of dexamethasone, a glucocorticoid, on the antitumor activity of CD8+ T cells in mice with B16 melanoma. Dexamethasone did not alter the antitumor efficacy of adoptive cell transfer (ACT)-based regimens. While dexamethasone decreased the number of native CD8+ splenocytes, it did not affect the numbers of CD8+ pmel-1 cells derived from ACT. Dexamethasone inhibited naive pmel-1 CD8+ cells but had little impact on activated cells'' proliferation and function. Glucocorticoids had a profound inhibitory effect on naive CD8+ T cells but had little impact on the proliferation and function of activated CD8+ pmel-1 T cells.',NULL,NULL,'2025-08-02 02:37:12.439651','https://journals.lww.com/00002371-200511000-00001',NULL,NULL,'cd8a_b4f9623ebd18e958',NULL,'not_reviewed'::public.review_status_enum,NULL,NULL),
	 ('The intrinsically trastuzumab-resistant cell line JIMT-1 showed CREB-mediated cell survival.',NULL,NULL,'2025-07-31 06:21:02.085056','https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/endocrinology/articles/10.3389/fendo.2022.1010092/full',NULL,NULL,'creb1_fbe246396f60ac21',NULL,'not_reviewed'::public.review_status_enum,NULL,NULL),
